      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Governments have a responsibility to protect their citizens from harm, and in cases of coordinated disinformation campaigns or domestic terrorism, state intervention is not only justified but necessary. The US model's hands-off approach can be too permissive, allowing malicious actors to exploit the internet for nefarious purposes. A more effective approach would be for governments to work with internet companies to develop and implement robust countermeasures, such as AI-powered content moderation and transparency reporting, to prevent and mitigate these threats.",
      "source": "target",
