    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but if we're talking about \"robust countermeasures\" and governments working with big tech to moderate content, isn't that basically just a fancy way of saying state-sponsored censorship? it feels like once you give a government the power to decide what counts as \"malicious\" or \"disinformation,\" they'll inevitably use it to crush any political opposition or keep themselves in power. how do you reconcile that risk with the idea of \"protecting\" citizens?",
